From 25fcbcc65fa547b59ddbec4c39ed67b742324d6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:03:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Transplant the yellow block from /cid to /cid/iwatchlist

Move the seven yellow sections off /cid, stopping before the cave.
/cid keeps the hero, Vivarium, portal band, flag block, Underground and
the cid-join gradient. /cid/iwatchlist takes the embed, the continuum,
the living wall, A Force of Nature, the forest and the canopy.

Untangle the state coupling first, since the build does not typecheck:

- New src/app/components/cid/: statcan-links.ts holds the shared SC link
  map (/cid keeps the underground cards, the subpage takes the
  continuum), plus DataAccessContinuum.tsx and LivingWallSlider.tsx,
  which were module-scope and unexported in CID.tsx. Disclosure,
  RouteItem, ROUTES, INDICATORS and SPECTRUM are used only by the
  continuum, so they travel with it.
- usePopulationModel moves to IWatchlist. It is a read-only hook with a
  24h cache, so no retained /cid section needs it.
- embedRef and its postMessage effect are deleted from CID.tsx; the
  subpage already had its own copy.
- roomRef stays on /cid with the Viv display room.
- lwSlide is dropped, not moved: it was set via onIndexChange and never
  read anywhere in the repo.

The portal band and the Innovation Watchlist flag block are signposts,
so they render on both pages. The flag is the red/white/red wl-flagrow
panel inside public/Innovation Watchlist.dc.html, reached through
section.cid-wl-hero, not a standalone asset.

CSS is imported, not forked: IWatchlist pulls cid-continuum, cid-forest
and cid-coins, and already renders inside .cid-scope.

Still open, pending Greg: the blue observatory lockup lives at the top of
the watchlist embed, so moving the embed takes the blue off /cid; the
Support CTA has no home and onSupport is still an unused prop on CID.

